Z||000000||rodmcneill||01-20-2001||12:06 AM||||This summer I want to install custom wheels on my 86GT. The wheels I have been looking at only come in 7" wide in a 16" wheel. This is fine for the front but for the rear I would like to install a 7 1/2" or 8" wide wheel to accept a slightly wider tire. This size only comes in a 17" wheel. I will probably run a 55 series tire front and a 50 series rear, does this combo of 16"-17" look okay? Any experience with this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||G-Nasty||01-20-2001||12:46 AM||||Looks great-16's in front 17's in rear...thats what i have on one of my GT's.<BR>I will e-mail you w/ a pic. I got the idea from the Acura NSX. You will have to lower the car with spindles and springs. I have koni up front and Bilstein in rear to keep it stiff. Good Luck-||||reg||1
